\section{Guarding against over-merging}{

Two different organizations can share an address (\verb{FIRST PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH}
and \verb{FIRST PRESBYTERIAN FOUNDATION} at one Boca Raton ZIP). Fuzzy clustering
therefore requires high name similarity \strong{and} applies npmatch's hard veto
predicates — conflicting embedded numbers, ordinals, or directions — so
\verb{LOCAL 32} never merges with \verb{LOCAL 45}, nor \code{FIRST} with \code{SECOND}. Inspect the
result with \code{\link[=pf_dedup_report]{pf_dedup_report()}} before trusting it.
